  "provenance": "Generated ONCE from the TypeScript buildPhysicPaintRotoProjectEqualitySource at 2026-11-06 (Phase 59-01). Frozen literals: any change must name which language moved and why. Never regenerate to make a failing parity test pass. 59-04 appended rail-motion and rail-motion-empty from the TypeScript authority (through parsePhysicPaintRotoPhysicalDocument) after the Rust encoder landed; the three 59-01 entries were not regenerated and their expected values did not move. 59-24 appended rail-motion-ordering, moved the TypeScript canonical ordering from ICU collation to code-unit order to match Rust's str::cmp, froze both new clips in the explicit persisted lifecycle shape (the shape both encoders read), and did not regenerate the five prior entries. 2026-11-07 (gap closure): appended rail-motion-exponent, a rail-motion clone whose scale key is 1e-7 and rotation key is 1e21. The TypeScript encoder moved to plain-decimal expansion (String(value) exponent form disagreed with Rust f64 Display); the six prior entries were not regenerated and their expected values did not move. 2026-11-07 (gap closure): every number now encodes as its IEEE-754 binary64 bit pattern (16 lowercase hex, big-endian) in BOTH languages. Decimal formatting forked the revision three ways — exponent notation (1e21 / 1e-7), negative zero (-0 vs 0), and shortest-roundtrip tie breaking (Rust half-away-from-zero vs ECMAScript half-to-even, e.g. -890236549097760.25). All seven entries were regenerated from the TypeScript authority together with their documents' revision strings; the semantic pins are unchanged (untouched and rail-motion-empty still share one project value). 2026-11-08 (261108-d5o): appended rail-motion-easings, a clone of rail-motion whose Position X opening key carries Linear and whose Rotation closing key carries Stop Motion, so both new easing tokens are frozen in the canonical source. The seven prior entries were not regenerated and their expected values did not move.",
